Package: hypercast
Type: Package
Title: Allocation-Free Casts of Scalars from Untrusted Text
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Brian", "Buvinghausen", email = "buvinghausen@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Skunk Werkx", role = "cph")
  )
Description: Parses booleans, characters, integers, reals, exact decimals, UUIDs,
    dates, times, date-times, durations, Unix and spreadsheet serial instants from text,
    under formats, field orders, precisions and epochs the caller declares rather than
    guesses. Every parse returns a verdict: the value, or a closed reason (empty,
    malformed, out of range) with the offending span of the input. The work is done by a
    compiled 'Rust' core shared with the project's bindings for other languages, which
    neither allocates nor panics. Every cast is vectorised and returns a data frame with
    one verdict per element; no cast signals an error for its data.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/SkunkWerkx/HyperCast
BugReports: https://github.com/SkunkWerkx/HyperCast/issues
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    jsonlite
